===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[fiddle]] with something in an [[attempt]] to [[fix]], [[mend]] or [[improve]] it, especially in an [[experimental]] or [[unskilled]] manner.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2012-01
|author=Robert M. Pringle
|title=How to Be Manipulative
|volume=100|issue=1|page=31
|magazine=[[w:American Scientist|American Scientist]]
|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2012/1/how-to-be-manipulative
|passage=As in much of biology, the most satisfying truths in ecology derive from manipulative experimentation. '''Tinker''' with nature and quantify how it responds.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To work as a tinker.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To tinker with; to [[tweak]] or attempt to fix.
#* {{w|G. K. Chesterton}}
#*: the broken bureau-lock and '''tinkered''' window-pane
#* '''2013''', Eric Goulard, ''Body Language Secrets Revealed''
#*: And because he wants to show that he is a dominant male, he '''tinkered''' the engine of his motorbike to make it even noisier.

